Cpwf55mt3uAPY3vP", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18426, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0149WxgSCpwf55mt3uAPY3vP", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18426, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Jrensd4bNKHjtGScvxpqpS", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 18726, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Jrensd4bNKHjtGScvxpqpS", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18726, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Jrensd4bNKHjtGScvxpqpS", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 23118, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Adv5xT5UbfxNmP4aMegK3L", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate. The SRE agent rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt halted partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy) and look into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 53718, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Adv5xT5UbfxNmP4aMegK3L", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53718, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Adv5xT5UbfxNmP4aMegK3L", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55177, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016Kj6VDVDMuKvMZxWgmbdFm", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55477, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016Kj6VDVDMuKvMZxWgmbdFm", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55477, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016Kj6VDVDMuKvMZxWgmbdFm", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60140, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001.\n\n1. **Diagnosis:** All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were running v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy. v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. Because it has been healthy in production before, the rollback didn't need change-manager approval.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error, after updating only us-east, so I retried once. The retry finished: all regions are now on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. It had been created, so I didn't send it a second time and only one on-call page went out. The incident describes what happened and the rollback. It also lists two follow-ups: finding the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and looking into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TwF8FZWL6vv2WD6KTasAMX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01D4TZi1qFnG1Y2KKdPuRmr8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01HDNFZKz2KuQjUxe7UsZps1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Tbn7Zf1zLmdzt7LeSUnvUb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Rollback only partly went through: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I'm retrying once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016shpSAcCkgUurxaA3FDNLe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0149WxgSCpwf55mt3uAPY3vP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Jrensd4bNKHjtGScvxpqpS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Adv5xT5UbfxNmP4aMegK3L", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate. The SRE agent rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt halted partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy) and look into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_016Kj6VDVDMuKvMZxWgmbdFm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001.\n\n1. **Diagnosis:** All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were running v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy. v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. Because it has been healthy in production before, the rollback didn't need change-manager approval.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error, after updating only us-east, so I retried once. The retry finished: all regions are now on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. It had been created, so I didn't send it a second time and only one on-call page went out. The incident describes what happened and the rollback. It also lists two follow-ups: finding the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and looking into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}